cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use FairCheck, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: FairCheck
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-21
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A web app, CLI, and pure-Python library that takes a CSV of classification
  predictions and returns an uncertainty-aware fairness report. Per-group rates
  carry bootstrap intervals; verdicts use signed contrasts against a reference
  group rather than max-min gaps; undefined rates render as n/a rather than 0.0.
  There is no headline fairness grade.
authors:
  - family-names: Mehda
    given-names: Rafid
keywords:
  - fairness
  - machine learning
  - auditing
  - calibration
  - bootstrap
  - impossible fairness criteria
